WEBVTT

00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:01.660
Some code is fragile for

00:00:01.700 --> 00:00:03.620
reasons the code doesn't show.

00:00:04.110 --> 00:00:07.480
Refactors of this function have broken error handling before.

00:00:07.930 --> 00:00:10.070
Mark it Refactor Sensitive,

00:00:10.600 --> 00:00:12.070
and the check asks for the reason.

00:00:12.670 --> 00:00:15.040
Record it as a memory: what went wrong,

00:00:15.040 --> 00:00:15.520
who owns it,

00:00:15.880 --> 00:00:18.390
and that the cause is still unexplained.

00:00:18.390 --> 00:00:19.330
Now it passes.

00:00:19.880 --> 00:00:22.140
Add a guard, and any declared change to

00:00:22.140 --> 00:00:24.730
the function needs a reevaluation.

00:00:24.960 --> 00:00:27.330
This refactor fails until someone reviews it.

00:00:27.880 --> 00:00:29.480
The reviewer records the outcome,

00:00:29.650 --> 00:00:30.980
the evidence and the date.

00:00:30.980 --> 00:00:32.180
The change passes.

00:00:32.730 --> 00:00:34.920
Shape checks that a review was recorded,

00:00:35.080 --> 00:00:36.610
not what it found.

00:00:36.610 --> 00:00:39.220
And no memory can waive a final forbid.
